<section class="prose"><p class="eyebrow">Evidence comparison · Sep 24, 2026</p><h1>DataForSEO vs SE Ranking API</h1>
<div class="notice"><strong>Comparison boundary:</strong> Search Data Benchmark #1 has not yet executed an identical workload across both providers. This page therefore compares the evidence we actually have and does not name an overall winner.</div>
<h2>Evidence available today</h2><table><tbody><tr><th>Area</th><th>DataForSEO</th><th>SE Ranking API</th></tr><tr><td>API surface</td><td>Official documentation verified</td><td>Hands-on API execution plus official documentation</td></tr><tr><td>Keyword-data execution in our evidence</td><td>NOT TESTED under SDB-B01</td><td>25 submitted; 23 data, 2 no-data in prior frozen run</td></tr><tr><td>SERP execution in our evidence</td><td>NOT TESTED under SDB-B01</td><td>6 fixed SERPs returned 10 rows each in prior frozen run</td></tr><tr><td>AI-search APIs</td><td>OFFICIAL DOCUMENTED</td><td>Not evaluated in the cited hands-on run</td></tr><tr><td>Comparable workload cost</td><td>UNRESOLVED</td><td>UNRESOLVED</td></tr></tbody></table>
<h2>What the evidence supports</h2><p>DataForSEO documents SERP, keyword-data and AI Optimization API families. SE Ranking has stronger hands-on evidence in our current archive because a prior frozen run executed keyword, SERP, rank-tracking, competitive and backlink tasks. That difference is an evidence-coverage difference, not proof that one provider is better.</p>
